      "rows": [
        [
          "Hand-written recursive descent (you've read C compiler source)",
          "Still the dominant production technique — clang/Roslyn/rustc/V8/tsc all do it"
        ],
        [
          "yacc/bison `.y` grammar files",
          "LALR(1) generators — the ACTION/GOTO tables are the LR automaton compiled to data"
        ],
        [
          "`System.Linq.Expressions` / expression trees",
          "A parsed AST is the same idea: a tree you walk; the parser is what builds it"
        ],
        [
          "Roslyn `SyntaxTree`, red-green nodes",
          "The output of an error-tolerant, incremental recursive-descent parser"
        ],
        [
          "Operator precedence in a calculator",
          "Pratt parsing / precedence climbing — binding powers replace one-function-per-level"
        ],
        [
          "Regex (regular) vs grammar (context-free)",
          "Lexer = regular = no nesting; parser = context-free = matched brackets, recursion"
        ]
      ]
    },
